      "look": {
        "female": true,
        "skin": "#d6a98a",
        "hair": "#2b1d14",
        "hairStyle": "long",
        "eyes": "#3e5a3a",
        "lips": "#a84a46",
        "age": 0.3,
        "tunic": "#22396a",
        "trim": "#c9a24a",
        "trousers": "#2e2a2a",
        "boots": "#2a2018",
        "belt": "#24170f",
        "cloak": "#7a1f22"
      },
      "outfit": {
        "helmet": true,
        "breastplate": true,
        "pauldrons": true,
        "sword": true
      },
      "dialogue": {
        "start": [
          {
            "if": [
              "met_captain"
            ],
            "node": "again"
          },
          {
            "node": "greet"
          }
        ],
        "nodes": {
          "greet": {
            "text": "Halt. You're not one of mine. State your business in the king's yard.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Just a traveller, Captain.",
                "next": "traveller"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'd like an audience with the king.",
                "next": "audience"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'm leaving."
              }
            ]
          },
          "again": {
            "text": "Back again? Walk with me if you're talking. I've a round to finish.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "What does the guard watch for?",
                "next": "watch"
              },
              {
                "text": "Tell me about your father.",
                "next": "father"
              },
              {
                "text": "Another time, Captain."
              }
            ]
          },
          "traveller": {
            "text": "Travellers are welcome in Valdren, so long as their hands stay where I can see them. Isolde Varn, Captain of the Guard, as my father was before me.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Your father was Captain too?",
                "next": "father"
              },
              {
                "text": "What does the guard watch for?",
                "next": "watch"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll keep my hands in sight."
              }
            ]
          },
          "audience": {
            "text": "The hall's straight ahead, and the king's mood is about as warm as the river in January. Mind your tongue in there.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Who are you, then?",
                "next": "traveller"
              },
              {
                "text": "Thanks for the warning."
              }
            ]
          },
          "watch": {
            "text": "Cutpurses on market days, drunks at the Broken Oar, wolves on the west road. And the old ruin by the forest, though there's nothing left in it but a hermit and bad memories.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "What happened at the ruin?",
                "next": "greywatch"
              },
              {
                "text": "A hermit?",
                "next": "hermit"
              },
              {
                "text": "Sounds quiet enough."
              }
            ]
          },
          "greywatch": {
            "text": "That was the Greywatch, Prince Edmund's tower. It burned in the Red Winter with the prince inside it. Brigands, the chronicle says. My father never said brigands. He never said anything at all.",
            "set": [
              "heard_tower_fire",
              "heard_edmund"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Your father was there?",
                "next": "father"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll let you get back to your round."
              }
            ]
          },
          "hermit": {
            "text": "Old man with a staff and a burned face. Lives by the ruin, comes to market twice a year, pays in honey. Harmless. The farm widow walks bread out to him.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "A burned face?",
                "next": "greywatch"
              },
              {
                "text": "Harmless. Good."
              }
            ]
          },
          "father": {
            "text": "Captain Aldous Varn. Led the guard thirty years and died last winter. Something weighed on him all that time. He drank to it every year, on the same night.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "The night the Greywatch burned?",
                "next": "night",
                "if": [
                  "heard_tower_fire"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Which night?",
                "next": "greywatch",
                "if": [
                  "!heard_tower_fire"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "I'm sorry for your loss.",
                "next": "sorry"
              }
            ]
          },
          "sorry": {
            "text": "Don't be. He had a long life and a short temper. Now, unless you need something, I've a gate to watch.",
            "leave": "Let her go."
          },
          "night": {
            "text": "Aye. After the funeral I found a letter in his chest, the royal seal broken on it. An order to arrest Prince Edmund. ‘Bring him alive,’ it said. Arrest, not rescue. Keep that to yourself.",
            "set": [
              "heard_arrest"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Who gave the order?",
                "next": "order"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll keep it quiet."
              }
            ]
          },
          "order": {
            "text": "King Harald's seal. And beneath it, the name of the officer who rode with my father to carry it out: Prince Osric. Our king.",
            "leave": "Say nothing more."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "smith",
      "name": "Brannoc",
      "role": "Blacksmith",
      "position": {
        "x": -11.3,
        "z": 34.6
      },
      "heading": 1.5708,
      "scale": 1.04,
      "action": "hammer",
      "look": {
        "skin": "#b07a58",
        "hair": "#2a1c12",
        "hairStyle": "bald",
        "beard": "short",
        "stubble": false,
        "eyes": "#5a4632",
        "age": 0.35,
        "belly": 0.45,
        "tunic": "#5e5a52",
        "trousers": "#3a3028",
        "boots": "#3a2a1e",
        "belt": "#2a1a10",
        "pouch": null,
        "trim": "#4a4038",
        "cloak": null
      },
      "outfit": {
        "apron": "#5a3a22",
        "hammer": true
      },
      "dialogue": {
        "start": [
          {
            "if": [
              "met_smith"
            ],
            "node": "again"
          },
          {
            "node": "greet"
          }
        ],
        "nodes": {
          "greet": {
            "text": "Mind the sparks. If you're buying, I've nails, hinges and a decent knife. If you're gawping, gawp from over there.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "What are you forging?",
                "next": "forging"
              },
              {
                "text": "Have you always been the smith here?",
                "next": "family"
              },
              {
                "text": "Just gawping. Sorry."
              }
            ]
          },
          "again": {
            "text": "Back for that knife, then?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Tell me again about the donjon door.",
                "next": "chains",
                "if": [
                  "heard_chains"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Your family made every lock in Valdren?",
                "next": "family",
                "if": [
                  "!heard_chains"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "What are you forging today?",
                "next": "forging"
              },
              {
                "text": "Not today."
              }
            ]
          },
          "forging": {
            "text": "Hinges for the chapel door. The chapel's stood empty since the old priest died, but the old hinges still scream like the damned when the wind gets in.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Have you always been the smith here?",
                "next": "family"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll let you work."
              }
            ]
          },
          "family": {
            "text": "Four generations at this anvil. My father, his father, and his before that. Every lock and chain in Valdren came out of this forge.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Every chain?",
                "next": "chains"
              },
              {
                "text": "Even the castle's?",
                "next": "castle"
              },
              {
                "text": "Impressive."
              }
            ]
          },
          "castle": {
            "text": "Gate hinges, portcullis teeth, the guards' mail. And the chains on the donjon door, though that was my father's work, not mine.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Tell me about those chains.",
                "next": "chains"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll leave you to it."
              }
            ]
          },
          "chains": {
            "text": "He forged them in a single night, the night after the Greywatch burned, with soldiers standing over him till dawn. He only spoke of it once, in his cups: ‘I locked bread away from hungry people.’",
            "set": [
              "heard_chains"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Bread? Behind that door?",
                "next": "bread"
              },
              {
                "text": "Why seal it at all?",
                "next": "why"
              },
              {
                "text": "A heavy thing to carry."
              }
            ]
          },
          "bread": {
            "text": "The royal granary is under the donjon. Has been since Queen Aldra's day. If there's grain in there after thirty years it's dust and rats. But that winter it was full. Full.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Why seal it at all?",
                "next": "why"
              },
              {
                "text": "Thank you, Brannoc."
              }
            ]
          },
          "why": {
            "text": "Ask the king, if you've the nerve. All I know is the lock has no key. My father melted it in this forge, on royal orders.",
            "leave": "Leave him to his hinges."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "maera",
      "name": "Maera",
      "role": "Keeper of the Broken Oar",
      "position": {
        "x": 11,
        "z": -7
      },
      "heading": 0,
      "action": "wipe",
      "look": {
        "female": true,
        "skin": "#e0b08e",
        "hair": "#7a3e1e",
        "hairStyle": "bun",
        "eyes": "#5a7a4a",
        "lips": "#b4504e",
        "age": 0.15,
        "tunic": "#3d6a4a",
        "sleeves": "#e8dcc4",
        "skirt": "robe",
        "trim": "#a8884a",
        "belt": "#4a3020",
        "pouch": null,
        "boots": "#3a2a1e",
        "cloak": null
      },
      "outfit": {
        "apron": "#ece4d2",
        "mug": true
      },
      "dialogue": {
        "start": [
          {
            "if": [
              "met_maera"
            ],
            "node": "again"
          },
          {
            "node": "greet"
          }
        ],
        "nodes": {
          "greet": {
            "text": "Welcome to the Broken Oar! Ale's brown, stew's hot, and the gossip's free. What'll it be, love?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Why ‘the Broken Oar’?",
                "next": "name"
              },
              {
                "text": "What's the gossip?",
                "next": "gossip"
              },
              {
                "text": "Just passing, thanks."
              }
            ]
          },
          "again": {
            "text": "Back already? Stew's still hot.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Any more gossip?",
                "next": "gossip"
              },
              {
                "text": "Sing me that song again.",
                "next": "ballad",
                "if": [
                  "heard_ballad"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Any songs worth hearing?",
                "next": "songs",
                "if": [
                  "!heard_ballad"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Later, Maera."
              }
            ]
          },
          "name": {
            "text": "Before the bridge there was a ferry, and the ferryman was Aldra's father. When she built the bridge she broke his oar over the first stone, so no one would ever pay to cross again. Or so my grandmother told it.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "What's the gossip?",
                "next": "gossip"
              },
              {
                "text": "A good story."
              }
            ]
          },
          "gossip": {
            "text": "Let's see. The smith's sweet on the miller's sister, the chapel hinges scream, and the king hasn't smiled since my mother was a girl.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Why doesn't the king smile?",
                "next": "king"
              },
              {
                "text": "Any songs worth hearing?",
                "next": "songs"
              },
              {
                "text": "Thanks, Maera."
              }
            ]
          },
          "king": {
            "text": "Lost his brother young. Prince Edmund, the one the old folk still raise a cup to when they think nobody's watching. Edmund of the Carts, they called him.",
            "set": [
              "heard_edmund"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Of the Carts?",
                "next": "carts"
              },
              {
                "text": "Any songs about him?",
                "next": "songs"
              }
            ]
          },
          "carts": {
            "text": "In the Red Winter, the story goes, he fed half the valley off the back of grain carts. Ask old Wynn at the farm. She was there; I was a babe in arms.",
            "set": [
              "heard_red_winter"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Any songs about him?",
                "next": "songs"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll ask her."
              }
            ]
          },
          "songs": {
            "text": "There's one. Not one I'd sing loud, mind; the guard broke a fiddler's fingers for it once. But you've an honest face.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Sing it. Quietly.",
                "next": "ballad"
              },
              {
                "text": "Never mind, then."
              }
            ]
          },
          "ballad": {
            "text": "♪ The king kept the bread in his tower of stone, / the prince drove the carts down the frost-bitten road; / they burned the grey watch with the prince in its keep, / but the valley remembers, and the valley won't sleep. ♪",
            "set": [
              "heard_ballad",
              "heard_edmund"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Who wrote it?",
                "next": "writer"
              },
              {
                "text": "Beautiful. Thank you."
              }
            ]
          },
          "writer": {
            "text": "Nobody knows. Some say a farm girl. Some say the hermit out by the ruin, though he's never once set foot in here. Pays in honey at the market, they tell me.",
            "leave": "Leave a coin on the bench."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tobias",
      "name": "Tobias Fenn",
      "role": "Merchant of Saltmere",
      "position": {
        "x": 13,
        "z": 10.6
      },
      "heading": -1.5708,
      "action": "behind",
      "patrol": {
        "mode": "pingpong",
        "speed": 1.1,
        "points": [
          {
            "x": 13,
            "z": 10.6,
            "wait": 9,
