      "look": {
        "skin": "#b88866",
        "hair": "#d8d4cc",
        "hairStyle": "long",
        "beard": "full",
        "eyes": "#4a6a8a",
        "age": 0.75,
        "scar": "burn",
        "tunic": "#5a4a38",
        "sleeves": "#4a3e30",
        "trousers": "#3a3228",
        "boots": "#2e2418",
        "belt": "#2a1e14",
        "pouch": "#5a4630",
        "trim": "#4a3e30",
        "cloak": "#4e5240"
      },
      "outfit": {
        "cowl": "#4e5240",
        "staff": true
      },
      "dialogue": {
        "start": [
          {
            "if": [
              "lore_complete",
              "!edmund_confessed"
            ],
            "node": "truth"
          },
          {
            "if": [
              "edmund_confessed"
            ],
            "node": "after"
          },
          {
            "if": [
              "met_hermit"
            ],
            "node": "again"
          },
          {
            "node": "greet"
          }
        ],
        "nodes": {
          "truth": {
            "text": "You have the look of someone who has been reading old stones. Well? Out with it.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "I know who you are. Edmund of the Carts.",
                "next": "confess"
              },
              {
                "text": "Not yet. Good day."
              }
            ]
          },
          "confess": {
            "text": "Edmund.” He is quiet for a long time. “Nobody has said that name to my face in thirty-one years. Aye. I opened my father's granary because Aldra's oath said I must, and because children were dying. They came to arrest me, my brother with them, and the fire came too. I crawled out through the cellar. Wynn found me on the road.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Why did you never go back?",
                "next": "why"
              },
              {
                "text": "Your brother has blamed himself ever since.",
                "next": "brother"
              }
            ]
          },
          "why": {
            "text": "Go back to what? A father who would have hanged me, and a kingdom ready to split in two over which son to follow. One dead prince was cheaper than a war. And the valley ate that winter. That was enough for me.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Your brother has blamed himself ever since.",
                "next": "brother"
              },
              {
                "text": "I understand.",
                "next": "brother"
              }
            ]
          },
          "brother": {
            "text": "Has he.” He looks down at his scarred hands. “Then tell him. Tell him the door can be opened now; there's no one left behind it to starve. And tell him I never blamed the boy.",
            "set": [
              "edmund_confessed"
            ],
            "leave": "Promise to tell the King."
          },
          "after": {
            "text": "Did you tell him? No, don't answer. I'll know soon enough if he comes.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "He will come.",
                "next": "come"
              },
              {
                "text": "Good night, Edmund."
              }
            ]
          },
          "come": {
            "text": "Then I had better find a second cup.” For the first time in a long while, he laughs. “Go on, now.",
            "leave": "Leave him by the fire."
          },
          "greet": {
            "text": "Hm. A visitor. Mind the fire, and mind the stones; the tower drops one now and then, to remind me it's still angry.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Who are you?",
                "next": "who"
              },
              {
                "text": "What is this place?",
                "next": "place"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll leave you be."
              }
            ]
          },
          "again": {
            "text": "Back by my fire? Sit, then. The crows are poor company.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Tell me about the night the tower burned.",
                "next": "burned"
              },
              {
                "text": "Who leaves heather on the prince's grave?",
                "next": "heather",
                "if": [
                  "lore_grave"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Just passing, old man."
              }
            ]
          },
          "who": {
            "text": "Nobody. An old man who keeps bees and talks to crows. The crows are better listeners.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "What is this place?",
                "next": "place"
              },
              {
                "text": "Your face is burned.",
                "next": "scar"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll leave you to your crows."
              }
            ]
          },
          "scar": {
            "text": "Fire is a careless sculptor.” He turns his cheek from the light. “Ask about the living, traveller. The burned have nothing to tell you.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "What is this place?",
                "next": "place"
              },
              {
                "text": "Forgive me."
              }
            ]
          },
          "place": {
            "text": "The Greywatch. It guarded the west road once, when Valdren still had something to guard it against. Now it guards me, and does a poor job of it.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "It burned, didn't it?",
                "next": "burned"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll leave you be."
              }
            ]
          },
          "burned": {
            "text": "In the Red Winter. Thirty-one years ago this winter. Brigands, they say in the town.",
            "set": [
              "heard_tower_fire"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "It wasn't brigands. It was the king's guard.",
                "next": "guard",
                "if": [
                  "heard_arrest"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "The prince's grave is empty. Even the song says so.",
                "next": "grave",
                "if": [
                  "lore_ballad"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Were you here then?",
                "next": "then",
                "if": [
                  "!heard_arrest",
                  "!lore_ballad"
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "I should go."
              }
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "text": "I have always been here, or it feels so. Go and talk to the living: the smith, the farm wife, the Captain. When you know more, come and tell me what you've learned.",
            "leave": "Leave him by the fire."
          },
          "guard": {
            "text": "Did they now.” He is quiet a long while. “Then you've spoken to a Varn. Old Aldous kept his silence longer than anyone deserved.",
            "set": [
              "hermit_trust"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "You knew Captain Varn?",
                "next": "varn"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll keep it to myself."
              }
            ]
          },
          "varn": {
            "text": "He carried an order he hated, from a king he feared, with a boy beside him who wanted to be anywhere else. The boy kicked in the door. The guard brought torches. Nobody meant the fire. Fire rarely asks.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "The boy was Osric.",
                "next": "osric"
              },
              {
                "text": "Thank you for telling me."
              }
            ]
          },
          "osric": {
            "text": "The boy ran into the flames after his brother and came out with his hand on fire and nothing in it. He has carried that empty hand ever since.” He stirs the embers. “Tell no one I said so.",
            "set": [
              "heard_osric_burn"
            ],
            "leave": "Promise, and go."
          },
          "grave": {
            "text": "Is it.” He smiles, and it doesn't reach his eyes. “Then whoever lies there is lighter than me, and luckier.",
            "set": [
              "hermit_trust"
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Do you leave the heather?",
                "next": "heather"
              },
              {
                "text": "I'll go."
              }
            ]
          },
          "heather": {
            "text": "Heather grows wild on the ridge. An old man walks; an old man picks. The dead don't mind.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "You're Prince Edmund.",
                "next": "deny"
              },
              {
                "text": "Of course. Good night."
              }
            ]
          },
          "deny": {
            "text": "Edmund of the Carts died in this tower with his father's bread on his conscience. I'm only the hermit who keeps his bees.” He looks at you a long while. “If you want the rest, find what the kingdom hid: the stones, the scrolls, the door. Then come back.",
            "set": [
              "hermit_challenge"
            ],
            "leave": "Leave him by the fire."
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
